### TikTok Business / TTO API smoke tests
###
### VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, replace the placeholder
### values below, then use "Send Request" above each request.
###
### Do not commit real client secrets or access/refresh tokens.

@tiktokBusinessBase = https://business-api.tiktok.com/open_api/v1.3
@tiktokOAuthBase = https://www.tiktok.com/v2/auth
@appBase = http://localhost:3000

@clientId = REPLACE_WITH_TIKTOK_BUSINESS_APP_ID
@clientSecret = REPLACE_WITH_TIKTOK_BUSINESS_APP_SECRET
@redirectUri = https://goheza.com/api/tiktok-business/callback
@authorizationCode = REPLACE_WITH_ONE_TIME_AUTH_CODE
@refreshToken = REPLACE_WITH_REFRESH_TOKEN
@accessToken = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
@creatorId = REPLACE_WITH_CREATOR_ID_OR_OPEN_ID
@videoId = REPLACE_WITH_TIKTOK_VIDEO_ID

### 1. Browser step: create an authorization URL
### Open the resulting URL in a browser. The authorization code is returned
### to @redirectUri and can only be used once.
###
### The exact scopes must be approved for the app in TikTok's portal.
### Remove any scope that TikTok has not approved for this app.
GET {{tiktokOAuthBase}}/authorize/?client_key={{clientId}}&scope=user.info.basic,user.info.profile,user.info.stats,video.list,video.publish,video.upload,biz.creator.info,biz.creator.insights,user.info.username,user.account.type,user.insights,video.insights&response_type=code&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}&state=replace-with-a-random-state

###
### 2. Exchange the authorization code for an access token
### The repo uses this endpoint in app/api/tiktok-business/callback/route.ts.
POST {{tiktokBusinessBase}}/tt_user/oauth2/token/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": "{{clientId}}",
  "client_secret": "{{clientSecret}}",
  "grant_type": "authorization_code",
  "auth_code": "{{authorizationCode}}",
  "redirect_uri": "{{redirectUri}}"
}

###
### 3. Refresh the access token
### TikTok may rotate the refresh_token; save the new one if returned.
POST {{tiktokBusinessBase}}/tt_user/oauth2/refresh_token/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": "{{clientId}}",
  "client_secret": "{{clientSecret}}",
  "grant_type": "refresh_token",
  "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###
### 4. Creator insights, including audience demographics
### This is the key request for audience countries, genders, and ages.
### Expected success shape: { "code": 0, "data": { ... } }
GET {{tiktokBusinessBase}}/tto/creator/authorized/?creator_id={{creatorId}}&fields=["handle_name","display_name","profile_image","bio","followers_count","following_count","videos_count","likes_count","creator_rate","country_code","content_labels","industry_labels","audience_countries","audience_genders","audience_ages","audience_devices","audience_usages"]
Access-Token: {{accessToken}}

###
### 5. Creator video analytics for one video
### The repository sends video_ids as a JSON-encoded query parameter.
GET {{tiktokBusinessBase}}/tto/creator/authorized/video/list/?creator_id={{creatorId}}&video_ids=["{{videoId}}"]
Access-Token: {{accessToken}}

###
### 6. Local app status: inspect the connected account and granted scopes
### Requires the app to be running and an authenticated browser session.
### In REST Client, cookies may need to be copied from browser DevTools.
GET {{appBase}}/api/tiktok-business/status

###
### 7. Local app creator insights proxy
### Uses the connected account stored in goheza_tests and refreshes its token.
### Requires the app's authenticated session.
POST {{appBase}}/api/tiktok-business/insights

###
### 8. Local app video analytics proxy
### Replace @videoUrl below if using the route instead of @videoId.
POST {{appBase}}/api/tiktok-business/analytics/video
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "videoId": "{{videoId}}"
}

###
### 9. Local app combined analytics proxy
### The route accepts either videoUrl or videoId. An empty body fetches the
### route's recent/combined behavior when supported by the connected account.
POST {{appBase}}/api/tiktok-business/analytics/combined
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "videoId": "{{videoId}}"
}

###
### 10. Standard TikTok API comparison: basic user stats
### This is not the Business/TTO demographic endpoint.
GET https://open.tiktokapis.com/v2/user/info/?fields=open_id,display_name,username,follower_count,following_count,likes_count,video_count
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###
### 11. Standard TikTok API comparison: basic per-video stats
### This returns views, likes, comments, and shares, not demographic data.
POST https://open.tiktokapis.com/v2/video/query/?fields=id,share_url,like_count,comment_count,share_count,view_count
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filters": {
    "video_ids": [
      "{{videoId}}"
    ]
  }
}
